[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32772"] :question/problem "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,-5,$ and $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-106963/selection/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer/id #uuid "97a26afb-340f-5904-8b26-108e5b552232" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106963/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "6ffa2433-d462-5391-bf51-7f5ca3498402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106963/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f88d63da-4453-54a7-95fa-67e8066bbca2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106963/selection/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" :answer/id #uuid "56167388-6202-54f2-b0b1-0