n is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 63 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 63 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,3,$ and $-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106959/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c159d750-ab1f-538b-b8cc-ae66ef1ae414"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106959"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106968/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "7af4998e-900e-5d3a-b2d0-5a67ba3c1bd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106968/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1f175b8f-1cb5-5081-8bab-32a0bbf07f94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106968/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "ee56c1fa-a2a4-56a0-bdc9-7e9489fabc6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106968/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "17949078-91cc-59ef-bc50-929a14f94bde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106968/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "56a43744-0df8-5e70-9317-4ff067fbb634" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106968/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "797eb4f8-5972-5720-931a-959a9248657f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106968/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-106968/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-106968/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-106968/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-106968/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-106968/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106968" :question/id #uuid "05cbbcd2-5089-5757-854c-7b38c52b8389" :question/math-academy-id "q-106968" :question/problem "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -32 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $-4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -32 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(-4)=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106968/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106968"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32726"] :question/problem "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{31}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{31}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}=-(-2)=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-105599/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "da85e6c1-0449-5189-bbe1-dbd3bf2d93d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" 