oxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(6)=-6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105599/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105599"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105601/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "dec51aba-8097-5e66-b19b-95856bef57c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105601/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0