U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(2)=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105601/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106966/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "8a763e28-b54e-56c9-88b0-217aa3c581d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106966/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "3768a685-f5c4-5e53-95bb-57d4f89d9639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/v