question/worked-solution "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{31}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{31}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}=-(-1)=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106966/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106966"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32749/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "da75fea9-1c0c-5fe4-b3ae-e4b340973606" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32749/selection/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799" :answer/id #uuid "005a5941-ce30-58dd-a948-23cbdcd2cd70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32749/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "edacba70-f391-5f2d-9561-37c8b7b5c7d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32749/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "d174d7f1-f66e-5dc3-91de-568809f7f6f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32749/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "325a0039-16df-5d56-94b5-0b26887833ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32749/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98183e62-5ad4-5d8b-88aa-29c5515d382f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32749/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-32749/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-32749/selection/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799" "q-32749/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-32749/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" "q-32749/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32749" :question/id #uuid "9ae12c41-39f0-5fcd-96aa-658aef468c29" :question/math-academy-id "q-32749" :question/problem "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\, & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${u}_{23}=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32749/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32749"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-105891"] :question/problem "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & 16 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-4$ and ${u}_{22}=-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-4)\\cdot (-4)=16.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-32652/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3601c22c-1f9c-5848-9713-1bc567dce25c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32652/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "18477d92-508d-58ef-bb16-e15737a20d74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32652/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "8436b6ed-45df-591a-81be-ee36d2226ded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32652/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "c1b9dc22-7f6f-5a7a-b95a-e14cd9d861d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32652/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "4863f28f-c43a-55e9-9d6f-264fe8a75890" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32652/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d76d4a34-5690-517b-87b3-9c407cd1ee2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32652/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-32652/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-32652/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-32652/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-32652/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" "q-32652/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32652" :question/id #uuid "08c00543-dc08-51a1-b8cb-9ed5911d188f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32652" :question/problem "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=-2$ and ${u}_{22}=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-2)\\cdot (-1)=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32652/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32741/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "36a85449-ff29-5185-a7bb-fb2b10283c40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32741/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b" :answer/id #uuid "1d564a76-9bdc-500a-8cba-1271f35798a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32741/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :answer/id #uuid "4f61c992-e720-5e43-88d6-a693052e62d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32741/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "b0adfd0f-7c8c-5b70-9dcc-ee3ca22d2eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32741/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "1fa8912d-1b6f-5f0c-8cc1-b69d8e5b2626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32741/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db808dac-1d58-5103-b59e-9e5dc3f4093d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32741/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer-field/choices ["q-32741/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-32741/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b" "q-32741/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" "q-32741/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" "q-32741/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32741" :question/id #uuid "378b5f3b-20b9-5362-adc1-3dbe1a5d125e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32741" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -10 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $B$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $B$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -10 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,5\\,\\, & 5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,5\\,\\, & 5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=5$ and ${u}_{23}=-3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=5\\cdot (-3)=-15.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32741/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32741"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105887/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "b37dbe8d-f63a-5b7f-bfac-2eb93b0c56b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105887/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "515bcff0-76a2-51b1-b24f-d6e697930a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105887/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer/id #uuid "0b54fefa-9dfc-5bf4-8d14-eab25d7744a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105887/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer/id #uuid "a82a4be4-e3e1-5d54-92f7-04e1751a2dd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105887/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" :answer/id #uuid "436dc45e-7153-5b4e-a337-efb927efcbec" :answer/type :answer.type/math 