3e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-107161/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107161" :question/id #uuid "3bca19d5-989a-5310-b9df-30c029c69158" :question/math-academy-id "q-107161" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $B=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $B$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{43}\\cdot {u}_{24}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $B$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & \\,2\\, & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & \\,2\\, & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{43}=-4$ and ${u}_{24}=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{43}\\cdot {u}_{24}=(-4)\\cdot (-6)=24.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-107161/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a86c24c2-97c2-534e-9c03-9735b031bb23"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107161"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105910/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a